          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is C (Answer Key: Topic 3, Q12). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t03-q013",
          "skill": "Inference",
          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "focus": "Draw logical deductions, extensions, or implications based on text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q13",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q13",
          "passage": "The Millennium Cohort Study (MCS) examines\ntrends in childhood development among 19,000\npeople in the United Kingdom unfolding over\nmany years. As is true of most longitudinal\nstudies, this need for years of data collection\nresults in high costs. By contrast, a relatively\nstraightforward fitness study, such as one that is\nmerely trying to identify the percentage of\nregular exercisers in a city who do weight\ntraining, may not need a large budget because",
          "prompt": "Which choice most logically completes the text?",
          "options": [
            "19,000 people is more than enough for\nMCS to find trends in childhood\ndevelopment.",
            "longitudinal methods are probably suitable\nfor the fitness study.",
            "the fitness study can be done well without\nyears of data collection.",
            "it would be easy for MCS researchers to\nadd questions to their childhood\ndevelopment study."
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is C (Answer Key: Topic 3, Q13). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t03-q014",
          "skill": "Inference",
          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "focus": "Draw logical deductions, extensions, or implications based on text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q14",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q14",
          "passage": "The small white heron and the little blue heron\nare long legged birds that live in wetlands, like\nthe Everglades in Florida. Laura D'Acunto and\ncolleagues wanted to know how these birds\nchoose an area in which to live. They looked at\nfeatures of these birds' habitats, such as how\nquickly water drains from the area and the\namount of tree-canopy cover there is in the area.\nThey found that small white herons prefer areas\nwith extensive canopy cover, but this was not\ntrue for little blue herons. The researchers\ntherefore concluded that wetland-management\nstrategies that increase the amount of tree\ncanopy in potential wetland bird habitats are\nless likely to",
          "prompt": "Which choice most logically completes the text?",
          "options": [
            "attract little blue herons to the area than\nthey are to attract small white herons to\nthe area.",
            "extend the average lifespan of small white\nherons already in the area than they are to\nattract a greater number of those birds to\nthe area.",
            "decrease the area's appeal to both small\nwhite herons and little blue herons than\nthey are to increase the appeal to other\nspecies.",
            "attract birds that don't typically live in\nwetlands to the area than they are to\nattract small white herons or little blue\nherons to the area."
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is A (Answer Key: Topic 3, Q14). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
        },
        {
          "id": "satoplam-t03-q015",
          "skill": "Inference",
          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "focus": "Draw logical deductions, extensions, or implications based on text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q15",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q15",
          "passage": "Architects looking for inspiration may examine\nphotographs of iconic buildings such as the\nLeaning Tower in Pisa. A two-dimensional\nphotograph, however, cannot capture how a\nbuilding interacts with its surroundings, whether\nby complementing, blending in with, or perhaps\neven clashing with sights and activities nearby.\nAn image of the Leaning Tower thus",
          "prompt": "Which choice most logically completes the text?",
          "options": [
