          "focus": "Draw logical deductions, extensions, or implications based on text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q26",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q26",
          "passage": "Quasars—such as APM 08279+5255, located in\nthe Lynx constellation—are extremely luminous\ngalactic nuclei powered by supermassive black\nholes, some of which are known to have\ndeveloped within the first billion years of the\nformation of the universe. Based on simulations\nthey conducted, astrophysicists Daniel Whalen,\nMuhammad Latif, and colleagues concluded\nthat these early quasars developed partly as a\nresult of rare convergences of gases in space\nwithout the need for ultraviolet backgrounds or\nother extreme and implausible environmental\nconditions that models of the early universe\nhave included to account for the presence of\nthese quasars. If this conclusion is correct, it\nsuggests that",
          "prompt": "Which choice most logically completes the text?",
