          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q33",
          "passage": "J.G. Ballard's 1984 novel Empire of the Sun\ncontains elements drawn from Ballard's own\nlife—there are many parallels between the\nexperiences of the novel's protagonist, Jim\nGraham, and those of Ballard, and as a result\nEmpire of the Sun is regularly described as an\nautobiographical novel. This characterization\ncan be useful, but it also presents drawbacks in\nterms of how the work is perceived, as it may\nlead readers to believe that Ballard merely\nfictionalized true events, which, in an artistic\nfield where creativity and inventiveness are\nprized, can suggest that",
