          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "focus": "Draw logical deductions, extensions, or implications based on text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q46",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q46",
          "passage": "Narwhals are shy whales that live in the remote\nArctic Ocean. Some of them have a long tusk,\nlike a unicorn horn, with sensitive nerves.\nNarwhals are known for this tusk, but many\nactually don't have one and its purpose is\nunknown. One group of scientists came up with\na possible purpose in 2014. The scientists\nsuggested that the tusk may help narwhals\ndetermine when water around them is likely to\nstart freezing and become dangerous for them.\nMarine biologist Kristin Laidre disagrees with\nthat idea, though. She reasons that if the\nnarwhal's tusk serves such an important\npurpose, then it's most likely that",
