          "passage": "Over 600 languages are spoken in New York\nCity in addition to English—one can find\nBartangi spoken in the neighborhood of\nYorkville, or Ghaile in Jackson Heights. Most\nspeakers of Chinese languages reside in the\nneighborhood of Flushing (part of New York\nCity's borough of Queens) and in Chinatown, in\nthe borough of Manhattan. New immigrants\nfrom north China, where Mandarin is the\nprimary first language, tend to settle in Queens,\nwhile new immigrants from south China, where\nmany people speak Cantonese or Fuzhounese as\na first language, tend to settle in Manhattan. It\ncan therefore be inferred that",
