            "Le Morte d'Arthur is more historically\naccurate than History, because Erec and\nEnide had not been written when Geoffrey\nof Monmouth was writing his work.",
            "Geoffrey of Monmouth's accounts of\nArthurian legends in his History are more\nsimilar overall in content to the accounts\nin Erec and Enide than they are to the\naccounts in Roman de Brut."
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is A (Answer Key: Topic 3, Q50). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
