          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q84",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q84",
          "passage": "Exclusively inhabiting tropical countries such as\nLiberia, wild chimpanzees lack adaptations to\nseasonal variations in ultraviolet B (UVB)\nirradiance from sunlight; since UVB exposure\nenables vertebrates to synthesize vitamin D, this\nraises questions about how chimpanzees in\nmid-latitude zoos are affected by the lower and\nmore variable UVB irradiance in those locations.\nIn a study of zoo chimpanzees in Norway and\nother mid latitude countries, Sophie Moittié and\ncolleagues found not only that chimpanzees'\nvitamin D levels correlate with UVB irradiance\nbut also that vitamin D levels show no evidence\nof plateauing as UVB irradiance reaches its\nhighest local levels, suggesting that",
          "prompt": "Which choice most logically completes the text?",
          "options": [
