        {
          "id": "satoplam-t03-q106",
          "skill": "Inference",
          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "focus": "Draw logical deductions, extensions, or implications based on text",
          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q106",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q106",
          "passage": "Biochemists I. Sam Saguy and Eli J. Pinthus\nstudied the mass and heat transfer processes\nthat occur when foods, such as the Indian\nsnacks makka poha and shankarpali, are fried in\noil. During frying, water in the crust evaporates,\nleaving voids that oil can fill, thereby increasing\nthe food's fat content. As the process continues,\nwater from the food's center moves to the crust\nas long as the crust remains permeable.\nTherefore, the less moisture a food loses during\nfrying,",
          "prompt": "Which choice most logically completes the text?",
          "options": [
            "the less the fat content is increased\nthrough frying.",
            "the higher the temperature must be to fry\nthe food.",
            "the slower the crust will lose its\npermeability.",
            "the crispier the crust will be when frying is\ncompleted"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Correct answer is A (Answer Key: Topic 3, Q106). Verified from SAToplam 2.0 Reading real exam compilation."
