          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 · Topic 3 · Q113",
          "passageTitle": "Inference — Q113",
          "passage": "Archaeologists have traditionally thought that\nmany cities in ancient Mesopotamia, including\nUruk and Ur, lay on the extremely dry banks of\nthe Tigris and Euphrates rivers. Jennifer\nPournelle and her team found evidence that the\nland these ancient cities sat on consisted of\nmarshy wetlands. This finding suggests that",
